Skip the 200 ms startup chime delay in U-Boot.

startup_buzz() enables the PWM channel, waits a fixed 200 ms so the chime is
audible, then disables it. Instrumented on the device it accounts for 200.1 ms
of board_late_init - the single largest item left in the pre-kernel stage after
the panel detection (0012, 34.5 ms measured the same way).

Opt-in so the chime can be brought back with one line in uboot.config.

diff --git a/boot/Kconfig b/boot/Kconfig
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -1319,6 +1319,14 @@
 	  Without that script the value is unused and the read costs ~200 ms.
 	  Keeps the VO power domain, the reset release and the DSI attach, so
 	  the panel is still initialised for scan-out.
+
+config RGXX3_SKIP_STARTUP_BUZZ
+	bool "Skip the U-Boot startup chime delay"
+	help
+	  startup_buzz() enables the PWM channel, sleeps a fixed 200 ms so the
+	  chime is audible, then disables it again. That delay is the largest
+	  single item in the pre-kernel stage on the RG353PS: 200.1 ms,
+	  measured with the bootstage marks from 0013.
 
 config BOOTSTAGE_STASH
 	bool "Stash the boot timing information in memory before booting OS"
diff --git a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
--- a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
+++ b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
@@ -232,6 +232,15 @@
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DM_PWM))
 		return;
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RGXX3_SKIP_STARTUP_BUZZ)) {
+		/*
+		 * The 200 ms below is a fixed delay for a chime, measured as
+		 * 200.1 ms of board_late_init on the RG353PS (bootstage marks
+		 * "late:led+buzz" -> "late:return").
+		 */
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* Probe the PWM controller. */
 	err = uclass_get_device_by_name(UCLASS_PWM,
 					"pwm@fe6e0010", &dev);
